Keep GPU rasterization off a GL that only pretends to have fences.

The 2in1 emulator draws the browser wrongly: stale tiles, tiles in the
wrong place, missing text, black bands along the bottom and right, worst
at 125% zoom and just after the UI changes shape. DevTools'
Page.captureScreenshot comes back entirely white. Turning off GPU
rasterization by hand -- the only variable changed -- fixes every one of
them, and GPU compositing is fine either way.

Its GL is ANGLE over the emulator's GLES over OpenGL 4.1 on Metal, and
that stack answers eglCreateSync with a failure and EGL_SUCCESS (0x3000)
as the error, which is to say it has no fence sync and does not admit it.
Rasterizing on the GPU then reads tiles that were never finished.

Matched on Metal in the renderer string, with no os clause. A real
HarmonyOS device has no Metal underneath it, so this cannot fire there --
and an os clause would do nothing anyway, which is its own problem:
GpuControlList::GetOsType() has no OHOS arm and falls through to kOsAny,
so every entry in both lists that names an operating system is inert on
this port. That is worth fixing on its own terms, not silently here,
because it would turn on a few hundred workarounds at once.

diff --git a/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json b/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
--- a/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
+++ b/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
@@ -186,7 +186,15 @@
       "gl_renderer": ".*PowerVR.*",
       "features": [
         "skia_graphite"
       ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": 190,
+      "description": "Emulator GL translated to Metal has no working fence sync; GPU rasterization reads unfinished tiles",
+      "gl_renderer": "(?i).*metal.*",
+      "features": [
+        "gpu_tile_rasterization"
+      ]
     }
   ]
 }
